IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp6-provinces-and-consent`
IMPORT `cp6-rates-review`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 112, 115 and 117 -- FINANCIAL STATEMENTS, THE CHIEF ACTUARY'S REPORT, THE ANNUAL REPORT.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2850 to 2864, 3036 to 3071 and 3073 to 3084 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 112: the Minister prepares annual financial statements, which the Auditor General audits. Section 115: every three years the Chief Actuary
-- reports on the Plan's finances and on the contribution rates that would pay for it; a further report follows a Bill that would change the
-- estimates; the report goes to the Minister of Finance, who lays it before the House of Commons. Section 117: the Ministers of Finance and of
-- Employment and Social Development report yearly on the administration of the Act to Parliament and the provinces.
--
-- THESE PROVISIONS ADDRESS OFFICIALS. They decide nothing a contributor can state a fact about, so the seat does not ask them (NOTES.md, seat).
-- They are encoded for what they require: who must do what, when the time runs, and which contents are mandatory.
-- The days Parliament sits are a calendar this encoding does not hold; the rules that count sitting days take them as a list.
-- Out of range, taken as inputs: the Investment Board Act (section 39(4)), the adjustment factors fixed under section 46(7) (piece cp3), the
-- calculation "in the prescribed manner" of the Chief Actuary's rates (no Regulation among the inputs prescribes it).
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the Minister's duty to prepare statements and the Auditor General's duty to audit (no holder of the claim named); the
-- Investment Board's duty to give the Auditor General records and the Auditor General's claim (s 112(4)); the Chief Actuary's duty to report and the
-- Minister of Finance's duty to lay the report; the Ministers' duty to table the annual report and to send it to the provinces, with the provinces'
-- claim to receive it (s 117(3)).

§ `Part III -- statements and reports (sections 112, 115 and 117)`

§§ `Not a provision: counting sitting days`

-- "on any of the first five days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting" (115(8)) and "on any of the first 15 days on which that House
-- is sitting after the report is prepared" (117(2)) both count sitting days after a date. The days are supplied in order, earliest first.
GIVEN after IS A DATE
      `the days on which the House sits, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
      number IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the first sitting days after a date` after `the days on which the House sits, earliest first` number MEANS
    take number (filter (GIVEN sitting YIELD sitting GREATER THAN after) `the days on which the House sits, earliest first`)

§§ `Section 112 -- annual financial statements`

-- src:2850 | Annual financial statements
-- src:2851 | 112 (1) The Minister shall, as soon as possible after the end of each fiscal year, prepare one set of annual financial statements for the Canada Pension Plan in respect of that year setting out
@ref Act s 112(1) (src:2850-2851)
GIVEN `the fiscal year has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(1) — the Minister must as soon as possible prepare one set of annual financial statements for the fiscal year` `the fiscal year has ended` MEANS
    `the fiscal year has ended`

-- src:2852 | (a) a statement combining the amounts credited to or charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account, the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the accounts of the Investment Board during the year;
-- src:2853 | (b) a schedule combining the amounts credited to or charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account and the accounts of the Investment Board in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan during the year;
-- src:2854 | (c) a schedule combining the amounts credited to or charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the accounts of the Investment Board in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan during the year;
-- src:2855 | (d) a statement combining the accounts of the Canada Pension Plan Account, the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the Investment Board as at the end of the year;
-- src:2856 | (e) a schedule combining the accounts of the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Investment Board in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan as at the end of the year;
-- src:2857 | (f) a schedule combining the accounts of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the Investment Board in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan as at the end of the year; and
-- src:2858 | (g) any other accounts and information that the Minister considers appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and the financial position of the Canada Pension Plan for the year.
@ref Act s 112(1)(a) to (g) (src:2852-2858)
DECLARE `cp6 Item of the annual financial statements` IS ONE OF
    `a statement combining the amounts credited to or charged to the two accounts and the accounts of the Investment Board during the year`
    `a schedule combining the base plan amounts credited or charged during the year`
    `a schedule combining the additional plan amounts credited or charged during the year`
    `a statement combining the accounts of the two accounts and the Investment Board as at the end of the year`
    `a schedule combining the base plan accounts as at the end of the year`
    `a schedule combining the additional plan accounts as at the end of the year`
    `any other accounts and information that the Minister considers appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and the financial position of the Canada Pension Plan for the year`
    `something else`

@ref Act s 112(1)(a) to (g) (src:2852-2858)
GIVEN item IS A `cp6 Item of the annual financial statements`
      `the Minister considers the accounts and information appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(1) — the annual financial statements must set out the item` item `the Minister considers the accounts and information appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and position` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `any other accounts and information that the Minister considers appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and the financial position of the Canada Pension Plan for the year` THEN
        `the Minister considers the accounts and information appropriate to present fairly the financial transactions and position`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:2859 | Reliance
-- src:2860 | (2) In preparing the annual financial statements, the Minister may rely on the annual financial statements prepared under subsection 39(4) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act.
-- out of range: subsection 39(4) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act (another Act, not deposited): whether the statements were prepared under it is a plain input.
@ref Act s 112(2) (src:2859-2860)
GIVEN `the financial statements were prepared under subsection 39(4) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) — the Minister may rely on the financial statements` `the financial statements were prepared under subsection 39(4) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act` MEANS
    `the financial statements were prepared under subsection 39(4) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`

-- src:2861 | Audit
-- src:2862 | (3) The annual financial statements of the Canada Pension Plan shall be audited annually by the Auditor General of Canada and a report of the audit shall be made to the Minister.
@ref Act s 112(3) (src:2861-2862)
GIVEN `the statements are the annual financial statements of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(3) — the statements must be audited annually by the Auditor General of Canada, who makes a report of the audit to the Minister` `the statements are the annual financial statements of the Canada Pension Plan` MEANS
    `the statements are the annual financial statements of the Canada Pension Plan`

-- src:2863 | Duty to provide information
-- src:2864 | (4) The Investment Board and its auditor shall provide the Auditor General of Canada with any records, accounts, statements or other information that in the opinion of the Auditor General of Canada are necessary to audit the annual financial statements of the Canada Pension Plan.
@ref Act s 112(4) (src:2863-2864)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Auditor General of Canada the records, accounts, statements or other information are necessary to audit the statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(4) — the Investment Board and its auditor must provide the records, accounts, statements or other information to the Auditor General of Canada` `in the opinion of the Auditor General of Canada the records, accounts, statements or other information are necessary to audit the statements` MEANS
    `in the opinion of the Auditor General of Canada the records, accounts, statements or other information are necessary to audit the statements`

§§ `Section 115 -- report of the Chief Actuary`

-- (1): "during the first year of each three-year period for which a review is required by subsection 113.1(1), ... as at a date not earlier than
-- December 31 of the year before the three-year period".
-- src:3036 | Report of Chief Actuary
-- src:3037 | Report of Chief Actuary
-- src:3038 | 115 (1) The Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions shall, during the first year of each three-year period for which a review is required by subsection 113.1(1), prepare a report setting out, as at a date not earlier than December 31 of the year before the three-year period, the results of an actuarial examination of the operation of this Act based on the state of the Canada Pension Plan Account, the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the investments of the Investment Board.
@ref Act s 115(1) (src:3036-3038)
GIVEN `the first year of the three-year period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the report is prepared` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which the results are set out` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1) — the Chief Actuary's report is prepared in time and as at a proper date` `the first year of the three-year period` `the day the report is prepared` `the date as at which the results are set out` MEANS
        DATE_YEAR `the day the report is prepared` EQUALS `the first year of the three-year period`
    AND `the date as at which the results are set out` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay ((`the first year of the three-year period`) MINUS 1) 12 31)

-- (1.1): the report must state estimates for each of the 30 years after the date of the examination ...
-- src:3039 | Contents of report
-- src:3040 | (1.1) The Chief Actuary shall, in the report,
-- src:3041 | (a) state, for each of the 30 years immediately following the date of the examination,
-- src:3042 | (i) the estimated revenues of the Canada Pension Plan Account and the estimated investment income of the Investment Board in respect of the base Canada Pension Plan, and the estimated amount of all payments under subsection 108(3), and
-- src:3043 | (ii) the estimated revenues of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account and the estimated investment income of the Investment Board in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan, and the estimated amount of all payments under subsection 108.2(3);
@ref Act s 115(1.1)(a) (src:3039-3043)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(a) — the number of years after the date of the examination for which the estimates are stated` MEANS 30

-- ... and, for each fifth year of a period of not less than 75 years from the date of the examination, an estimate of the percentage required.
-- src:3044 | (b) state, for each fifth year of a period of not less than 75 years from the date of the examination, an estimate of the percentage of total contributory salaries and wages and contributory self-employed earnings that would be required to provide for all payments under subsection 108(3) in that year if there were no balance in the Canada Pension Plan Account at the commencement of that year and the Investment Board had no investments;
@ref Act s 115(1.1)(b) (src:3044)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(b) — the least number of years from the date of the examination in the period` MEANS 75

@ref Act s 115(1.1)(b) (src:3044)
GIVEN `the number of years after the date of the examination` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of years in the period, not less than the least` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.1)(b) — an estimate of the percentage is stated for the year` `the number of years after the date of the examination` `the number of years in the period, not less than the least` MEANS
        `the number of years after the date of the examination` AT LEAST 5
    AND (`the number of years after the date of the examination`) MODULO 5 EQUALS 0
    AND `the number of years after the date of the examination` AT MOST `the number of years in the period, not less than the least`
    AND `the number of years in the period, not less than the least` AT LEAST `s 115(1.1)(b) — the least number of years from the date of the examination in the period`

-- (c), (d) and (e): a contribution rate for self-employed persons (base), a first additional rate and a second additional rate, each "for each year of a
-- period of not less than 75 years after the three-year period in which the report is prepared".
-- src:3045 | (c) in respect of the base Canada Pension Plan, specify a contribution rate calculated, in respect of self-employed persons for each year of a period of not less than 75 years after the three-year period in which the report is prepared, by combining
-- src:3046 | (i) a contribution rate, calculated in the prescribed manner, without taking into account the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) for which the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph (ii) exceeds zero, and
-- src:3047 | (ii) a contribution rate calculated in the prescribed manner in respect of the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) in respect of the base Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:3048 | (c.1) [Repealed, 2016, c. 14, s. 52]
-- src:3049 | (d) in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan, specify a first additional contribution rate calculated, in respect of self-employed persons for each year of a period of not less than 75 years after the three-year period in which the report is prepared, by combining
-- src:3050 | (i) a first additional contribution rate, calculated in the prescribed manner, without taking into account the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) for which the first additional contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph (ii) exceeds zero, and
-- src:3051 | (ii) a first additional contribution rate calculated in the prescribed manner in respect of the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) that affect the first additional contribution rate;
-- src:3052 | (e) in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan, specify a second additional contribution rate calculated, in respect of self-employed persons for each year of a period of not less than 75 years after the three-year period in which the report is prepared, by combining
-- src:3053 | (i) a second additional contribution rate, calculated in the prescribed manner, without taking into account the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) for which the second additional contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph (ii) exceeds zero, and
-- src:3054 | (ii) a second additional contribution rate calculated in the prescribed manner in respect of the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) that affect the second additional contribution rate;
-- src:3055 | (f) specify the rates referred to in subparagraphs (c)(i) and (ii), (d)(i) and (ii) and (e)(i) and (ii) and set out the manner in which those rates were calculated.
@ref Act s 115(1.1)(c) to (f) (src:3045-3055)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(c) to (e) — the least number of years after the three-year period for which each rate is specified` MEANS 75

-- (c), (d) and (e): each rate is specified "by combining (i) a contribution rate, calculated in the prescribed manner, without taking into account the
-- changes ... referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e) ... and (ii) a contribution rate calculated in the prescribed manner in respect of the changes".
-- "Combining" is read as adding (fork C6-F20): section 113.1(11.05) tests the self-employed rate less the (c)(ii) rate against the (c)(i) rate, which
-- is the same as testing it against their sum. The manner of calculation is "prescribed" and no Regulation among the inputs prescribes it, so
-- (i) and (ii) are inputs, in fractions.
@ref Act s 115(1.1)(c) (src:3045-3047)
GIVEN `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(c) — the contribution rate specified for self-employed persons for the base Canada Pension Plan` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` MEANS
    (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`) PLUS (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`)

@ref Act s 115(1.1)(d) (src:3049-3051)
GIVEN `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(d) — the first additional contribution rate specified for self-employed persons` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` MEANS
    (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`) PLUS (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`)

@ref Act s 115(1.1)(e) (src:3052-3054)
GIVEN `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 115(1.1)(e) — the second additional contribution rate specified for self-employed persons` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` `the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)` MEANS
    (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (i), without the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`) PLUS (`the rate calculated under subparagraph (ii), in respect of the changes referred to in paragraph 113.1(4)(e)`)

-- The contents the subsection requires, paragraph by paragraph: "(f) specify the rates referred to in subparagraphs (c)(i) and (ii), (d)(i) and (ii) and
-- (e)(i) and (ii) and set out the manner in which those rates were calculated."
@ref Act s 115(1.1) (src:3039-3055)
DECLARE `cp6 Content of the Chief Actuary's report under subsection 115(1.1)` IS ONE OF
    `the estimated revenues, investment income and payments for the base Canada Pension Plan for each of the 30 years`
    `the estimated revenues, investment income and payments for the additional Canada Pension Plan for each of the 30 years`
    `an estimate of the percentage of contributory salaries and wages and contributory self-employed earnings required in each fifth year`
    `the contribution rate specified for self-employed persons for the base Canada Pension Plan`
    `the first additional contribution rate specified for self-employed persons`
    `the second additional contribution rate specified for self-employed persons`
    `the rates referred to in paragraphs (c) to (e) and the manner in which they were calculated`
    `something else`

@ref Act s 115(1.1) (src:3039-3055)
GIVEN content IS A `cp6 Content of the Chief Actuary's report under subsection 115(1.1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.1) — the Chief Actuary must state the content in the report` content MEANS
    CONSIDER content
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Subsection 115(1.1)(c.1) (line 3048) is repealed in this text and states nothing.

-- (1.11): "In the first report prepared after 2015 and in every third report that follows, the Chief Actuary shall specify ... the factors as
-- calculated according to a methodology that he or she considers appropriate; the Chief Actuary may also, if he or she considers it
-- necessary, specify the factors in any report prepared under subsection (1) after 2015."
-- src:3056 | Adjustment factors
-- src:3057 | (1.11) In the first report prepared after 2015 and in every third report that follows, the Chief Actuary shall specify, in reference to the adjustment factors fixed under subsection 46(7), the factors as calculated according to a methodology that he or she considers appropriate; the Chief Actuary may also, if he or she considers it necessary, specify the factors in any report prepared under subsection (1) after 2015.
@ref Act s 115(1.11) (src:3056-3057)
GIVEN `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.11) — the Chief Actuary must specify the adjustment factors in the report` `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` MEANS
    `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` AT LEAST 1
    AND ((`the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report`) MINUS 1) MODULO 3 EQUALS 0

@ref Act s 115(1.11) (src:3056-3057)
GIVEN `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Actuary considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.11) — the Chief Actuary may specify the adjustment factors in the report` `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` `the Chief Actuary considers it necessary` MEANS
    `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report` AT LEAST 1
    AND (   `s 115(1.11) — the Chief Actuary must specify the adjustment factors in the report` `the number of the report counting from the first report prepared after 2015, 1 for that report`
         OR `the Chief Actuary considers it necessary`)

-- (1.2): the relation between the rates is the one subsection 113.1(7)(a) and (b) states (cp6-rates-review.l4).
-- src:3058 | Relationship between rates
-- src:3059 | (1.2) For the purposes of the calculations referred to in paragraphs (1.1)(c) to (e),
-- src:3060 | (a) the rates for employees and employers for a year must be identical; and
-- src:3061 | (b) the rates for self-employed persons for a year must be equal to the sum of the rates for employees and employers for that year.
@ref Act s 115(1.2) (src:3058-3061)
GIVEN `the rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.2) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` `the rate for employees for the year` `the rate for employers for the year` `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` MEANS
    `s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` `the rate for employees for the year` `the rate for employers for the year` `the rate for self-employed persons for the year`

-- (1.3): "Subsection 114(4) applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the making of the regulations prescribing the manner
-- of the calculation ... and to the making of any regulation changing that manner of calculation."
-- src:3062 | Application of subsection 114(4)
-- src:3063 | (1.3) Subsection 114(4) applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the making of the regulations prescribing the manner of the calculation referred to in paragraphs (1.1)(c) to (e) and to the making of any regulation changing that manner of calculation.
@ref Act s 115(1.3) (src:3062-3063)
GIVEN `the number of included provinces` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent` IS A NUMBER
      `the population of all the included provinces` IS A NUMBER
      `the population of the included provinces that have signified consent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(1.3) — the regulations prescribing the manner of the calculation may be made or changed` `the number of included provinces` `the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent` `the population of all the included provinces` `the population of the included provinces that have signified consent` MEANS
    `s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` `the number of included provinces` `the number of included provinces whose lieutenant governor in council has signified consent` `the population of all the included provinces` `the population of the included provinces that have signified consent`

-- src:3064 | Report when certain Bills introduced
-- src:3065 | (2) In addition to any report required under subsection (1) and in accordance with a request of the Minister of Finance, whenever any Bill is introduced in the House of Commons to amend this Act in a manner that would in the opinion of the Chief Actuary materially affect any of the estimates contained in the most recent report made under that subsection, the Chief Actuary shall prepare a report as set out in subsection (3).
@ref Act s 115(2) (src:3064-3065)
GIVEN `a Bill is introduced in the House of Commons to amend this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Chief Actuary the Bill would materially affect any of the estimates in the most recent report under subsection 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Finance has requested the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(2) — the Chief Actuary must prepare a report on the Bill` `a Bill is introduced in the House of Commons to amend this Act` `in the opinion of the Chief Actuary the Bill would materially affect any of the estimates in the most recent report under subsection 115(1)` `the Minister of Finance has requested the report` MEANS
        `a Bill is introduced in the House of Commons to amend this Act`
    AND `in the opinion of the Chief Actuary the Bill would materially affect any of the estimates in the most recent report under subsection 115(1)`
    AND `the Minister of Finance has requested the report`

-- (3): the same assumptions and basis as the most recent report, "and using, in addition, other actuarial assumptions and another basis if the
-- Chief Actuary is of the opinion that these other actuarial assumptions and the other basis more accurately reflect a change in demographic or
-- economic circumstances".
-- src:3066 | Contents of report
-- src:3067 | (3) A report that is prepared under subsection (2) in respect of a Bill shall set out the extent to which the Bill would, if enacted by Parliament, materially affect any of the estimates contained in the most recent report made under subsection (1), using the same actuarial assumptions and basis that were used in that report and using, in addition, other actuarial assumptions and another basis if the Chief Actuary is of the opinion that these other actuarial assumptions and the other basis more accurately reflect a change in demographic or economic circumstances since the most recent report made under subsection (1) was prepared.
@ref Act s 115(3) (src:3066-3067)
GIVEN `the Chief Actuary is of the opinion that other assumptions and another basis more accurately reflect a change in demographic or economic circumstances since the most recent report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(3) — the report on the Bill must also use other actuarial assumptions and another basis` `the Chief Actuary is of the opinion that other assumptions and another basis more accurately reflect a change in demographic or economic circumstances since the most recent report` MEANS
    `the Chief Actuary is of the opinion that other assumptions and another basis more accurately reflect a change in demographic or economic circumstances since the most recent report`

-- Subsections 115(4) to (7) (line 3068) and section 116 (line 3071) are repealed in this text and state nothing.

-- (8): "if Parliament is then sitting, [on receipt]; or if Parliament is not then sitting, on any of the first five days next thereafter that
-- Parliament is sitting, and if at the time any report under this section is received by the Minister of Finance Parliament is then dissolved, the
-- Minister of Finance shall forthwith cause a copy of the report to be published in the Canada Gazette."
-- src:3069 | Report to be laid before House of Commons
-- src:3070 | (8) Forthwith on the completion of any report under this section, the Chief Actuary shall transmit the report to the Minister of Finance, who shall cause the report to be laid before the House of Commons forthwith on its receipt if Parliament is then sitting, or if Parliament is not then sitting, on any of the first five days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting, and if at the time any report under this section is received by the Minister of Finance Parliament is then dissolved, the Minister of Finance shall forthwith cause a copy of the report to be published in the Canada Gazette.
DECLARE `cp6 State of Parliament when the Minister of Finance receives the report` IS ONE OF
    `Parliament is then sitting`
    `Parliament is then not sitting`
    `Parliament is then dissolved`

DECLARE `cp6 Way the Minister of Finance must make the report public` IS ONE OF
    `lay it before the House of Commons forthwith on its receipt`
    `lay it before the House of Commons on any of the first five days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting`
    `cause a copy to be published in the Canada Gazette forthwith`

@ref Act s 115(8) (src:3069-3070)
GIVEN state IS A `cp6 State of Parliament when the Minister of Finance receives the report`
GIVETH A `cp6 Way the Minister of Finance must make the report public`
`s 115(8) — the way the Minister of Finance must make the report public` state MEANS
    CONSIDER state
    WHEN `Parliament is then sitting` THEN `lay it before the House of Commons forthwith on its receipt`
    WHEN `Parliament is then not sitting` THEN `lay it before the House of Commons on any of the first five days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting`
    WHEN `Parliament is then dissolved` THEN `cause a copy to be published in the Canada Gazette forthwith`

@ref Act s 115(8) (src:3069-3070)
GIVEN `the day the Minister of Finance receives the report` IS A DATE
      `the days on which Parliament sits, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 115(8) — the day is one of the first five days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting` `the day the Minister of Finance receives the report` `the days on which Parliament sits, earliest first` day MEANS
    elem day (`the first sitting days after a date` `the day the Minister of Finance receives the report` `the days on which Parliament sits, earliest first` 5)

§§ `Section 117 -- annual report to Parliament and the provinces`

-- src:3073 | Annual Report to Parliament and the Provinces
-- src:3074 | Annual report to be made by Ministers
-- src:3075 | 117 (1) The Minister of Finance and the Minister of Employment and Social Development shall, as soon as possible after the end of each fiscal year, together prepare a report on the administration of this Act during that year, including
-- src:3076 | (a) the annual financial statements for that year prepared under section 112 and the report of the Auditor General of Canada on those statements;
-- src:3077 | (b) the number of contributors during that year and the number of persons to whom benefits were payable during that year; and
-- src:3078 | (c) any other information that the Ministers, and the appropriate provincial Ministers of the participating provinces, as defined in section 2 of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act, consider appropriate.
@ref Act s 117(1) (src:3073-3078)
GIVEN `the fiscal year has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) — the Ministers must as soon as possible together prepare a report on the administration of the Act during the year` `the fiscal year has ended` MEANS
    `the fiscal year has ended`

@ref Act s 117(1)(a) to (c) (src:3075-3078)
DECLARE `cp6 Item of the annual report on the administration of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the annual financial statements for the year under section 112 and the report of the Auditor General on those statements`
    `the number of contributors during the year and the number of persons to whom benefits were payable during the year`
    `any other information that the Ministers and the appropriate provincial Ministers consider appropriate`
    `something else`

@ref Act s 117(1)(a) to (c) (src:3075-3078)
GIVEN item IS A `cp6 Item of the annual report on the administration of the Act`
      `the Ministers and the appropriate provincial Ministers of the participating provinces consider the information appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) — the annual report must include the item` item `the Ministers and the appropriate provincial Ministers of the participating provinces consider the information appropriate` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `any other information that the Ministers and the appropriate provincial Ministers consider appropriate` THEN
        `the Ministers and the appropriate provincial Ministers of the participating provinces consider the information appropriate`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (2): "on any of the first 15 days on which that House is sitting after the report is prepared".
-- src:3079 | Tabling in Parliament
-- src:3080 | (2) The Ministers shall cause the report to be laid before each House of Parliament on any of the first 15 days on which that House is sitting after the report is prepared.
@ref Act s 117(2) (src:3079-3080)
GIVEN `the day the report is prepared` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the House sits, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 117(2) — the day is one of the first 15 days on which the House sits after the report is prepared` `the day the report is prepared` `the days on which the House sits, earliest first` day MEANS
    elem day (`the first sitting days after a date` `the day the report is prepared` `the days on which the House sits, earliest first` 15)

-- src:3081 | Presentation to provinces
-- src:3082 | (3) As soon as possible after the report is prepared, the Ministers shall send the report to the appropriate provincial Minister of every province.
@ref Act s 117(3) (src:3081-3082)
GIVEN `the report has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 117(3) — the Ministers must as soon as possible send the report to the appropriate provincial Minister of every province` `the report has been prepared` MEANS
    `the report has been prepared`

-- src:3083 | Definition of appropriate provincial Minister
-- src:3084 | (4) In this section, appropriate provincial Minister, in respect of a province, means the province’s minister of the Crown who has primary responsibility for that province’s finances.
@ref Act s 117(4) (src:3083-3084)
GIVEN `the minister is the province's minister of the Crown who has primary responsibility for that province's finances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 117(4) — the minister is the appropriate provincial Minister of the province` `the minister is the province's minister of the Crown who has primary responsibility for that province's finances` MEANS
    `the minister is the province's minister of the Crown who has primary responsibility for that province's finances`
